# Commits that changed formatting and nothing else. `git blame` skips them and
# attributes each line to the commit that last changed its meaning.
#
# Turn it on once per clone — git does not read this file by default:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub's blame view reads it automatically and needs no configuration.
#
# Only add a commit here if it is genuinely behaviour-free. A commit that
# reformatted *and* fixed something makes the fix invisible to blame forever,
# which is worse than the noise it was meant to remove.

